    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1978867479146332377",
      "url": "https://x.com/thecryptoBike/status/1978867479146332377",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/thecryptoBike/status/1978867479146332377",
      "text": "Privacy Rabbit Hole Recap\n\nZcash on Aztec & The Future of Programmable Privacy\n\nHosts & Guests\n@realRoberto38, @clairekart , @0xdavid \n\nSpeakers:\n@bajpaiharsh244 \n@zmanian \n@Zac_Aztec \n@clairekart \n\nLets Get started:\n1⃣ Harsh’s Presentation “ZEC on Aztec”\n\n• Context: Why Zcash\n\n• Launched 2016, PoW chain, 21M cap like BTC.\n\n• Privacy at the base layer, shielded transactions.\n\n• Endorsed by Edward Snowden, Naval: “If Bitcoin is insurance against fiat, Zcash is insurance against Bitcoin’s publicity.”\n\n• Zashi wallet: easy private payments; “encrypted burritos” joke during demo.\n\n• Aztec Overview\n\n• Aztec = Private World Computer, just like Ethereum was the “world computer” for Bitcoin’s base layer.\n\n• Combines Zcash-style privacy + Ethereum programmability.\n\n• Supports private smart contracts, partial privacy, public–private composability.\n“You choose what parts of your program you want to keep private or public.”\n\n2⃣ Zcash → Aztec Bridge Concept\n\n• Problem: current Zashi + Near intents swaps leak metadata (sender/receiver visible).\n\n• Aztec solution: “Partial Notes”, lets users receive funds without revealing their address.\n\n- Alice → sends ZEC privately to a solver.\n- Solver → sends USDC to Alice’s partial note on Aztec.\n- Solver never learns Alice’s Zcash or Aztec address.\n- No link between chains, full unlinkability.\n\n• Future: Wrapped ZEC on Aztec\n\n- Trustless bridge → mint wZEC on Aztec.\n\n- Allows private DeFi for ZEC: lending, liquidity, yield.\n\n- Can be secured via EigenLayer AVS or fully-ZK light clients.\n“ZEC holders could earn yield privately while maintaining full censorship resistance.”\n\n• Demo Summary\n\n• Live Zcash testnet swap → Aztec local node.\n\n• Initial solver lacked balance → fixed mid-demo.\n\n• Successful private swap confirmed (“Congratulations, your private swap is successful”).\n\n• Applause from chat: “3,600 people watching privacy in action!”\n\n3⃣ Fireside Chat — Zaki Manian × Zach × Claire\n\nOrigins of Privacy\n\n• Zaki:\n\n- Privacy = essential to censorship resistance.\n\n- Bitcoin lacks privacy → risk of “good vs. bad BTC.”\n\n- Early 2010s talk with Aaron (ZeroCash) → “This is magic.”\n\n- Zashi wallet = 2% → 20–30% shielded usage.\n\n- Near intents + cross-chain swaps = “finally real privacy for real users.”\n\n• Zach:\n\n- Started in 2017 building DeFi (CreditsMint) → realized no privacy = no real finance.\n\n- Bitcoin’s “pseudonymity” was illusion.\n\n- Studied Zcash papers, became a self-taught cryptographer.\n“Back then, understanding ZK was hell — now you can learn in a weekend.”\n\n• why Optional Privacy\n\n• Zaki:\n\n- Practical + compliance reasons: exchanges need transparent TX support.\n\n- Gemini = only exchange supporting shielded deposits.\n\n- Binance required a unique “transparent-only” address type to stay listed.\n\n• Zach:\n\n• For Aztec, optional privacy is programmability & trust trade-off:\n- Private users shouldn’t inadvertently help bad actors hide.\n\n- Hybrid models allow transparent protocols + private users.\n\n- Fully private DEXes need advanced MPC/FHE tech — not production-ready yet.\n\n• Cross-Chain & Future of Privacy\n\n• Zaki:\n\n- “2025–2026 is the first time the rubber meets the road for private systems.”\n\n- Two privacy paths:\na) Encrypted balances (limited, enterprise use).\n\nb) Full private layers (like Aztec & Zcash).\n\n- Zcash aims to remain a private store-of-value, Aztec provides programmable privacy.\n\n• Claire: Why is privacy booming now?\n\n• Zach:\n\n- “Blockchain’s protest phase is over. Now it’s institutional, and institutions need privacy.”\n\n- “Either they fork chains privately or they adopt privacy-preserving layers like Aztec.”\n\n• Zaki:\n\n- “Privacy matters most to whales & institutions — those with real capital to protect.”\n\n- “If you’re running a DeFi protocol, you can’t reveal every trade on-chain. Privacy becomes business-critical.”\n\n4⃣ Community Activation\n\n• Zaki announced a Zashi onboarding event:\n\n- Roles eligible: Illuminated and Paragon.\n- Participants install Zashi → receive small ZEC drop directly from him.\n“A surprise mini-airdrop, real ZEC for real privacy users.”\n\n• Rebranding: Town Hall → Privacy Rabbit Hole\n\n• Claire:\n\n“Aztec believes Privacy must win. Not just Aztec, the entire movement.”\n\n- Town Hall renamed to “Privacy Rabbit Hole” → open forum for all privacy builders (ECC, EF, Monero, etc.).\n\n- Future guests will include Ethereum Foundation privacy leads and other ecosystems.\n\n5⃣ Community Awards (Discord Names)\n• Meme Lord\n\n- HellforNDR → recurring meme favorite (“No airdrop, still love you”).\n\n• Maestros\n\n- Web3 Genio → IRL Aztec flyers, stickers, meetups — “Privacy is the future.”\n\n- Caperson (Sui Swap) → short-form news-style Aztec explainer videos.\n\n- Ayana (Philippines) → Honk Skater Boy art.\n\n- Yelena → surreal Honk x tentacle digital art timelapse.\n\n• Content Chronicler\n\n- NotBored (Opay Me DeFi) → regular video explainers tagged.\n\n• Operator Roles\n\n- Proposer Commander: Boss7140\n\n- High Attester: AgeSaints\n\n- Homestaker Sentinel: Pavel M0542\n\n6⃣ Final Stats & Announcements\n\n• Snapshot recorded: 4,662 attendees.\n\n• IRL Meetups: Continuing in Philippines, Thailand, Indonesia, Vietnam, Nigeria, Argentina.\n\n• Zashi onboarding: live in Paragon & Illuminated channels.\n\nNext Privacy Rabbit Hole: Ethereum Foundation guest + Aztec ecosystem collabs.",
